  "output": {
    "answer": "No inter-rater reliability number exists for the 87-lot set. The caveats note is explicit: truth is my taps only, one tapper, EN-heavy, five UTC days of streams, and it flags a selection bias risk — I likely tap more when a pick is clearly right or clearly wrong than when it's ambiguous. There's no second labeler or re-shuffled re-check run against this set in the record, and no stated reason why a held-out labeler wasn't used — that part isn't in the record. A separate experiment (EXP-E35a, card-number legibility) did re-present crops to the same labeller for a stability check, but that's a different dataset and explicitly not inter-rater agreement either.",
